      "links_hash": "sha256:abf59b51979334a652048212b88955c9cd333edd24f9cb1d01162726be829a0e",
      "subtitle": "So long as the bulk of China’s imports from the United States (and many others) are bought by state firms, China has the ability to manage its trade. The management isn’t new. What’s new is Trump’s implicit willingness to accept managed trade so long as the trade is managed in a way that is judged to help the United States.",
